      "instructions": "1-6: Complete the form below. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER for each answer.\n7-10: Answer the questions below. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS for each answer.",
      "transcript": "EUAN: Good morning, Northbank Community Allotments. Euan speaking. How can I help?\nISLA: Hello. My name is Isla MacLeod. I moved to the west end recently, and I'd like to put my name down for a plot. I saw two sites on the council page, but I wasn't sure which one currently accepts applications.\nEUAN: Both accept names for their waiting lists. Riverside is larger and has conventional plots, while Northbank has several smaller spaces and raised beds. Which location would suit you?\nISLA: I first thought Riverside because it's near the bus route. Actually, after checking the walking distance from my flat, Northbank is closer, so please put Northbank as my preferred site.\nEUAN: Certainly. The smaller plots there are popular with new growers. Would you like a standard ground plot, or one of the raised beds? A raised bed is easier to manage, though it has less growing space.\nISLA: The raised bed, please. I work full time, so a smaller area is sensible for my first season. I can always apply for a standard plot later if I manage it well.\nEUAN: We ask members to name one day when they will usually visit. It doesn't stop you coming on other days; it simply helps us plan volunteer cover. At present we have cover on Tuesday, Thursday and Saturday.\nISLA: Saturday sounds convenient, but that's when I often visit my parents. Tuesday is much more reliable because I finish work early, so enter Tuesday as my regular day.\nEUAN: Good. Membership isn't a casual weekly arrangement. New members make a minimum commitment, then renew if they want to continue. The fee is collected every six months, but the commitment itself is longer.\nEUAN: The minimum membership period is twelve months. That gives people enough time to prepare the bed, plant it and complete a full growing cycle.\nISLA: That's fine. I own small hand tools, but I don't have room at home for anything bulky. Does the communal shed have equipment members can borrow?\nEUAN: Yes. Spades, forks and watering cans are stored there. We have two wheelbarrows as well, but because they're in demand I need to mark one large item on your form. Shall I record a wheelbarrow?\nISLA: Yes, a wheelbarrow would be the useful one. I can bring my own fork and trowel. What happens before I get the gate code?\nEUAN: You attend a short induction. The next one was advertised for the seventh of May, but that session filled yesterday. We've added another on the fourteenth of May, and I can reserve you a place then.\nISLA: The fourteenth works. Is the induction held in the tool shed? I noticed a small classroom on the site map as well.\nEUAN: The classroom is used once the tour starts, and the shed comes later when we explain tool returns. Don't go to either place first, because the gate may still be locked.\nEUAN: Meet me at the main gate. I'll check the attendance list there and take the group inside together.\nISLA: Right. Should I bring the confirmation email, or is the reference number enough?\nEUAN: Neither is necessary because your name will be on my list. Please bring photo ID, though. We must confirm the person receiving the gate code is the applicant.\nISLA: No problem. I was planning to wear old shoes. Do I need to buy safety glasses or heavy boots before the session?\nEUAN: Closed shoes are enough for the induction, and safety glasses aren't needed for the basic tour. We provide gardening gloves, so don't buy those specially. Just choose a pair when you arrive.\nISLA: Thanks. If my train is delayed that morning, should I call this office number?\nEUAN: The office is closed on induction mornings. Email the volunteer team instead; one of them monitors that inbox from half past eight and can tell you whether the group has entered the site.\nISLA: Great. I have everything I need for the application and the induction. That all sounds manageable.\nEUAN: Excellent. I’ll send the application link this morning. If anything is unclear, just reply to that message.",
